  <h2>Is SimLocal or Yesim the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with SimLocal if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want the cheaper plan for a single trip</li>
        <li>You're heading to the UK and want a real local number for calls and texts</li>
        <li>You'd rather cancel for any reason than rely on a narrower "unused plan" refund</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with Yesim if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You travel repeatedly and want a balance that carries over instead of resetting</li>
        <li>You want a refund guarantee that explicitly covers a plan you bought but never used</li>
        <li>You're fine paying more per day for that flexibility</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The two refund policies aren't the same guarantee.</strong> SimLocal's "No Quibble Refunds" policy lets you cancel and get your money back without justifying why. Yesim's 30-day money-back guarantee is narrower: it covers plans that go unused, not a change of mind after you've already started using one. If unconditional cancellation matters more to you than the refund window, that difference matters.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Only one of them gives you an actual phone number.</strong> Most SimLocal UK plans bundle a real UK number for calls and texts, which we confirmed by buying one ourselves. Yesim is data-only; voice has to go through an app like WhatsApp or Viber over the data connection, the same as most other eSIMs on this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>SimLocal vs Yesim FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, SimLocal or Yesim</h3>
      <p>SimLocal. It sits in our "Cheap" price bracket, while Yesim sits in "Expensive." Yesim's higher price pays for its rollover balance and broader refund guarantee, not for being the better deal on a single trip.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does either one include a real phone number</h3>
      <p>SimLocal does on most UK plans: a full UK number for calls and texts, confirmed by buying one ourselves. Yesim is data-only, with no bundled number.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which has the better refund policy</h3>
      <p>It depends what you need. SimLocal's "No Quibble Refunds" policy lets you cancel for any reason, no explanation needed. Yesim's 30-day money-back guarantee only covers plans you never actually used, which is narrower but still better than providers that only refund a plan that never connected at all.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can unused data roll over to my next trip on either one</h3>
      <p>Only on Yesim. Its Pay &amp; Fly balance carries over between trips by design. SimLocal sells a fixed plan that expires 14 days after purchase with no rollover.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

